# Enter a general application

A clerk records a paper N244 against an existing TEC PCN case. The application is a row on that case, not a new CCD case and not a case link. Submitting the event does not change the PCN `CaseState`.

The caseworker journey, starting from the Case details tab, is on the design docs site: [Enter a general application](http://localhost:4567/caseworker-journeys.html#journey-enter-a-general-application).

## Where the event appears

| | |
| --- | --- |
| Event id | `enterGeneralApplication` |
| Display name | Enter a general application |
| Who can run it | Clerk (`caseworker-tec`), create, read, and update |
| When | Every `CaseState` |
| Feature flags | None |
| Case state after submit | Unchanged. The submit response sets a confirmation body and does not call `.state()` |

The local authority role is not granted the event. The desired-matrix “Make N244 application” action for a local authority is a different, unimplemented event.

The state diagram’s `generalApplicationReceived` arrows are not this event and are not implemented.

## Form

`TecCaseConfiguration.configureEnterGeneralApplication` registers the event. The form is `GeneralApplicationEntry`, unwrapped onto the case with the `genApp` prefix (`@JsonUnwrapped(prefix = "genApp")`). Page show conditions need top-level case field ids, so conditions use ids such as `genAppApplicationType` and `genAppFeeReceived`.

The event uses `.showSummary()`, so ExUI shows check your answers before submit.

| Page | Shown when | Fields |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Application details | Always | Who made the application (Local authority or Respondent), date received, type (Adjourn, Set aside, or Something else). Categories is a text area and appears only for Something else. |
| Hearing date | Type is Adjourn | Whether there is a hearing in the next 14 days. This does not create or change a hearing. |
| Application fee | Always | Whether HMCTS has received the fee. Amount is required when the answer is Yes. A label is shown when the answer is No. Help with Fees, and the reference when that answer is Yes. |
| Application consent and notice | Always | Whether all parties consent. Without notice is required when they do not. |
| Upload general application | Always | The N244 document. Required. |
| Upload related evidence | Always | Optional collection of documents. |
| Refer without notice application to judge | Parties do not consent and the application is without notice | Label: “You must refer this application to a judge.” The page does not send a referral. |

Applicant is a fixed list because TEC has no party records to choose from.

### Validation

Continuing from Application details fails when the received date is today or in the future: “Date the application was received must be in the past”.

Continuing from Application fee, and submit, both fail unless the fee has been received: “You must request payment from the applicant before entering this application”. The clerk records a fee that has already been taken. There is no card payment and no service request.

Submit repeats those rules and also requires the conditional fields (categories, hearing question, amount, Help with Fees reference, without notice) and a complete N244 document (url, binary url, and filename).

## What is stored

Flyway `V23__create_tec_case_general_application.sql` creates `public.tec_case_general_application`, one row per application, many per `tec_case`. `TecCaseRepository.insertGeneralApplication` assigns `rank` as one more than the current maximum for that case, and always stores state `GEN_APP_ISSUED` (`GeneralApplicationState`, label “Issued”). Yes/no answers are stored as the enum name.

Documents are separate rows in `tec_case_document`, written by `storeGeneralApplicationDocuments`:

- the N244 uses Case File View category `applications` (Applications)
- each related evidence file uses `uncategorisedDocuments` (Uncategorised)

Document URLs are rewritten with `CdamDocumentUrls.toCdamUrl` before insert.

The event form is not persisted on the case. `TecCaseView.getCase` clears `generalApplication` and rebuilds the `generalApplications` collection from `findGeneralApplications`, ordered by rank. Case details shows that collection, including state, only when it is not empty. The section label is **General applications**.

The confirmation panel is titled **Application entered** and includes the case number. The “What happens next” text says that a without-notice application informs only the applicant, and any other application informs all parties. Nothing in this event sends that correspondence or creates a work-allocation task.
